{
 "esm": "1.1.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "NoahSnowmeltSoilWaterCoupling",
  "description": "Coupling library (esm-spec section 10.9) handing WRF Noah's snow-surface energy balance to its soil-water transport: the melt rate becomes the water supply at the soil surface. Roles: Col (the assembly), Sno (`snow_energy.esm`, SNOPAC's closure and melt rate) and Sm (`soil_moisture.esm`). THE SINGLE LOAD-BEARING EDGE IS Sno.ex -> Sm.melt, which is WRF's `PRCP1 = PRCP1 + EX` in SNOPAC: the melt joins the supply at exactly the point rain does and therefore goes through the same canopy split, and on a melting pack it dominates everything else -- 8.0e-7 m/s at the strongest step of the cold-season set, against a bare-ground column's dew of order 1e-9. THE SECOND EDGE IS EASY TO MISS AND IS NOT COSMETIC: `dew_to_soil` = 0. NOPAC does PRCP1 = PRCP1 + DEW, so frost on bare ground infiltrates; SNOPAC sets DEW = -ETP1 and never adds it to PRCP1, because under a pack the frost is deposited on the SNOW and reaches the soil only later, as melt. Leaving the transport's snow-free default in place would silently add that frost to the soil twice over -- about 6 % of the total liquid tendency at the frost column this library is tested on. Verified against the reference: prcpf*0.001 + ex reproduces SNOPAC's own PRCP1 BITWISE at all 67 snow-covered steps of the cold set. Import with coupling_import + bind {Col, Sno, Sm}.",
  "tags": [
   "coupling-library",
   "wrf",
   "land-surface",
   "noah",
   "snowmelt",
   "soil-moisture",
   "param_to_var"
  ]
 },
 "coupling_roles": {
  "Col": {
   "description": "The assembly. Owns the snow-surface forcing, tells the transport it is under a pack, and receives the melt rate, the branch indicator and the total water supply."
  },
  "Sno": {
   "description": "Noah snow-surface energy balance (SNOPAC's closure); provides the melt rate ex and the branch indicator melting."
  },
  "Sm": {
   "description": "Noah soil moisture; its melt and dew_to_soil parameters are driven from here, and it reports the total surface water supply prcp1_eff."
  }
 },
 "coupling": [
  {
   "type": "variable_map",
   "from": "Col.sfctmp",
   "to": "Sno.sfctmp",
   "transform": "param_to_var",
   "description": "sfctmp into the snow-surface energy balance"
  },
  {
   "type": "variable_map",
   "from": "Col.th2",
   "to": "Sno.th2",
   "transform": "param_to_var",
   "description": "th2 into the snow-surface energy balance"
  },
  {
   "type": "variable_map",
   "from": "Col.t1_in",
   "to": "Sno.t1_in",
   "transform": "param_to_var",
   "description": "t1_in into the snow-surface energy balance"
  },
  {
   "type": "variable_map",
   "from": "Col.rch",
   "to": "Sno.rch",
   "transform": "param_to_var",
   "description": "rch into the snow-surface energy balance"
  },
  {
   "type": "variable_map",
   "from": "Col.rr",
   "to": "Sno.rr",
   "transform": "param_to_var",
   "description": "rr into the snow-surface energy balance"
  },
  {
   "type": "variable_map",
   "from": "Col.t24",
   "to": "Sno.t24",
   "transform": "param_to_var",
   "description": "t24 into the snow-surface energy balance"
  },
  {
   "type": "variable_map",
   "from": "Col.fdown",
   "to": "Sno.fdown",
   "transform": "param_to_var",
   "description": "fdown into the snow-surface energy balance"
  },
  {
   "type": "variable_map",
   "from": "Col.flx2",
   "to": "Sno.flx2",
   "transform": "param_to_var",
   "description": "flx2 into the snow-surface energy balance"
  },
  {
   "type": "variable_map",
   "from": "Col.emissi",
   "to": "Sno.emissi",
   "transform": "param_to_var",
   "description": "emissi into the snow-surface energy balance"
  },
  {
   "type": "variable_map",
   "from": "Col.df1",
   "to": "Sno.df1",
   "transform": "param_to_var",
   "description": "df1 into the snow-surface energy balance"
  },
  {
   "type": "variable_map",
   "from": "Col.snowh",
   "to": "Sno.snowh",
   "transform": "param_to_var",
   "description": "snowh into the snow-surface energy balance"
  },
  {
   "type": "variable_map",
   "from": "Col.sncovr",
   "to": "Sno.sncovr",
   "transform": "param_to_var",
   "description": "sncovr into the snow-surface energy balance"
  },
  {
   "type": "variable_map",
   "from": "Col.prcp",
   "to": "Sno.prcp",
   "transform": "param_to_var",
   "description": "prcp into the snow-surface energy balance"
  },
  {
   "type": "variable_map",
   "from": "Col.snowing",
   "to": "Sno.snowing",
   "transform": "param_to_var",
   "description": "snowing into the snow-surface energy balance"
  },
  {
   "type": "variable_map",
   "from": "Col.esd",
   "to": "Sno.esd",
   "transform": "param_to_var",
   "description": "esd into the snow-surface energy balance"
  },
  {
   "type": "variable_map",
   "from": "Col.dt_pack",
   "to": "Sno.dt_pack",
   "transform": "param_to_var",
   "description": "dt_pack into the snow-surface energy balance"
  },
  {
   "type": "variable_map",
   "from": "Col.etanrg",
   "to": "Sno.etanrg",
   "transform": "param_to_var",
   "description": "etanrg into the snow-surface energy balance"
  },
  {
   "type": "variable_map",
   "from": "Col.esnow_rate",
   "to": "Sno.esnow_rate",
   "transform": "param_to_var",
   "description": "esnow_rate into the snow-surface energy balance"
  },
  {
   "type": "variable_map",
   "from": "Sno.ex",
   "to": "Sm.melt",
   "transform": "param_to_var",
   "description": "THE EDGE THIS LIBRARY EXISTS FOR: the snow-energy component's melt rate becomes the transport component's surface water supply, which is WRF's PRCP1 = PRCP1 + EX"
  },
  {
   "type": "variable_map",
   "from": "Col.dew_to_soil",
   "to": "Sm.dew_to_soil",
   "transform": "param_to_var",
   "description": "tell the transport that it is running UNDER A PACK, where SNOPAC deposits frost on the snow instead of routing it into the soil"
  },
  {
   "type": "variable_map",
   "from": "Sno.ex",
   "to": "Col.ex_in",
   "transform": "param_to_var",
   "description": "expose the melt rate for assertion"
  },
  {
   "type": "variable_map",
   "from": "Sno.melting",
   "to": "Col.melting_in",
   "transform": "param_to_var",
   "description": "expose which SNOPAC branch the energy balance selected"
  },
  {
   "type": "variable_map",
   "from": "Sm.prcp1_eff",
   "to": "Col.water_supply_in",
   "transform": "param_to_var",
   "description": "expose the total liquid water the transport actually sees"
  }
 ]
}
